body:
**Found by** the flip re-check and the full in-house qualification on the merged image (dev-soft-core 59b09884, 8x8/1if). It is a DUT failure; no failure is acceptable for the lab.

**Observed:** after a link-up, the DUT's first ENTITY_AVAILABLE comes **5.76 to 6.82 s** after its first frame. The controller's discovery wait is the entity's declared discovery time, 6.0 s, so several scenarios fail "the DUT was not discovered within 6.0 s".
- In the re-check's runs (3 of 5), each slow case had a grandmaster change about 4 to 5 s after link-up.
- In pass A of the full qualification, 5 scenarios failed on it; pass B has more instances so far.

**Expected:** ADP advertises the entity as soon as its interface is up (IEEE 1722.1-2021 6.2.4 Advertising Entity State Machine and 6.2.5 Advertising Interface State Machine: the interface advertises on a link-state change to up, and separately on a grandmaster update; the variables linkIsUp and advertisedGrandmasterID drive those transitions). Milan v1.2's ADP rules and the gPTP grandmaster change (4.2.x) must not hold back the first ENTITY_AVAILABLE past the declared discovery time. A grandmaster change is announced by a new ENTITY_AVAILABLE; it is not a reason to wait.

**Where to look:** the split firmware's ADP start after LINK (`sw/firmware/ctrl/`), and whether the first advertise waits for asCapable, the grandmaster, or a settle timer; the link-up debounce in the platform.

**Acceptance:**
- the first ENTITY_AVAILABLE within the entity's **declared discovery time** of link-up, with Milan's prescribed draws (0 to 4 s at DOWN to LINK_UP, 0 to 2 s at start-up; Milan v1.2 5.6.3.5.2 and 5.6.3.5.3, uniform per IEEE 1722.1-2021 6.2.4.2.2), at 1x1/1if and 8x8/1if, with and without a grandmaster change during the first 6 s (corrected 2026-11-22 by the ruling in this issue; the earlier "within 1 s" was an error);
- the declared 6.0 s derived and stated in FR_NFR (draw + link publication + loop passes + PHY link time);
- the grandmaster change still announced (a new ENTITY_AVAILABLE with the new gptp_grandmaster_id);
- a host test of both orders with a planted defect;
- the bench re-run of the affected scenarios.

Relates to #665.
